  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run, using 1 of the 6 runs: all 5 witnesses got their expected verdicts, and the rule uses all 9 names the node claims.\n\n**How the rule reads the node:**\n- **Who it covers:** a pedestrian under `DEF-NRS-484A-165::pedestrian`.\n- **When it applies:** the pedestrian is now on a highway and off every sidewalk, and has stayed that way since a moment when they were on a sidewalk of that highway, moving, with an obstruction within `p.obstruction_encounter_reach` of their body.\n- **Exception (c):** the rule does not apply while the pedestrian is in a bicycle lane or path with an obstruction within the same reach.\n- **The duty:** the pedestrian's body stays within `p.pedestrian_detour_offset` of the sidewalk they left. The obligation writes out the whole sidewalk-and-highway selection again, as rule 3c requires.\n\nI added no narrowings of my own; every span is written the way the node maps it.\n\n**Witnesses** (a barrier blocks the sidewalk, and the pedestrian leaves it at t = 0):\n- **forbid:** walks 4 m from the sidewalk → violated.\n- **permit:** walks 0.5 m from it, then returns → compliant.\n- **idle:** never leaves the sidewalk → not applicable.\n- **blind:** same as forbid with `st.region_geometry` masked → unknown.\n- **branch_1:** walks in a bicycle lane 3 m from the sidewalk, with a second barrier 0.5 m away → not applicable.\n\nI only changed the two files I own.\n\nFiles are in `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke31-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent`:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_297_6_o2.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_297_6_o2.lean`\n- `results/smoke31-1111-0039/iter-001/code/NRS_484B_297_6_o2/task_result.md`",
